<?php
/**
 * Spartrak (LTR) override of Smartwave_Porto's html/head.phtml.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Porto's own head.phtml renders 11 render-blocking
 * <link> tags — 4 Google Fonts requests, bootstrap, animate.css, a
 * header-type stylesheet, custom.css, and the two DB-generated
 * configed_css files. It is injected into the `head.additional` container
 * (Smartwave/porto's Smartwave_Porto/layout/default.xml), i.e. AFTER every
 * layout-declared <css src>, so those files also outranked this theme's own
 * stylesheets on load order.
 *
 * Measured against the live site (homepage, PDP, category, search), none of
 * it earns its place — this theme replaces Porto's markup wholesale with
 * .spartrak-* BEM (header.phtml / footer.phtml / product/list.phtml), so
 * Porto's CSS is styling elements that are no longer rendered:
 *
 *   css/header/type1.css      1.7KB    0.0% of selectors match live markup
 *   configed_css/design_*     19.4KB  11.7%   (Porto theme_color #ff6840)
 *   custom.css              109.3KB  13.8%
 *   bootstrap.min.css        52.9KB   1.7%   (15 utility classes, and the
 *                                             only live consumer is Porto's
 *                                             display:none newsletter popup)
 *   configed_css/settings_*  10.8KB  26.8%   (see var/porto-custom-style.bak.css)
 *   4x fonts.googleapis.com           Open Sans (requested TWICE by Porto),
 *                                     Oswald, Poppins — none of which appear
 *                                     in _typography.less's font stack
 *                                     (thmanyah sans / Inter / Inter Tight).
 *
 * Total removed: ~194KB uncompressed of render-blocking CSS plus 4 extra
 * DNS+TLS+request round-trips to a third-party host, on a connection the
 * origin currently serves over HTTP/1.1 (so those requests contend for the
 * ~6-connection-per-host budget rather than multiplexing).
 *
 * The colour/typography that Porto was supplying is the design system's job
 * — see web/css/spartrak-foundations.less. The handful of Porto rules that
 * were still load-bearing were migrated to
 * web/css/source/components/_porto-chrome.less.
 *
 * ALSO DROPPED: Porto's sticky-header script. It bound an unthrottled
 * scroll+resize handler that queried and mutated `.page-header` — an element
 * this theme does not render (`.page-header` survives in the live HTML only
 * inside that script's own jQuery selector strings). It was pure scroll-time
 * cost for no effect. Sticky behaviour, if wanted, belongs in this theme's
 * own header JS.
 *
 * ALSO DROPPED: the `pt_animate` bootstrap and its [data-plugin-animate] /
 * [data-appear-animation] sweep, together with animate.css (19.4KB). Only 4
 * elements on the sampled pages carry those attributes, all inside Porto
 * furniture, and `.animated` never appears in the rendered output.
 *
 * KEPT: js_porto_vars / window.theme / redirect_cart — these are read by
 * Porto JS modules that are still in the bundle and cost nothing.
 *
 * @var \Smartwave\Porto\Block\Template $block
 */
$porto_helper = $this->helper('Smartwave\Porto\Helper\Data');
$_redirect_cart = $porto_helper->getConfig('checkout/cart/redirect_to_cart');
?>
<script type="text/javascript">
window.theme = {};
var js_porto_vars = {};
var redirect_cart = <?= $_redirect_cart ? 'true' : 'false' ?>;
</script>
